TestJob6.vtt (Amazon Transcribe)
Pros
Output Type: Batch: StartTranscriptionJob/   Streaming: StartStreamTranscription, StartStreamTranscriptionWebSocket
Speaker Labels: More conversational, includes greetings and context (e.g., "good afternoon, Saria. Welcome to our branch.").
Natural Language: Captures filler words ("uh", "um"), making it closer to real speech.
Simple Numbering: Uses sequential numbers for each caption, making it easy to follow.
Short Segments: Breaks dialogue into shorter, more readable lines.
Cons
No Speaker Names: Does not explicitly label who is speaking.
Filler Words: Includes many filler words, which may reduce readability for some use cases.
Less Structured: Lacks unique IDs or metadata for each segment.
Potential Typos: Some lines are incomplete or have minor errors (e.g., "N" at the end).



